    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65848" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελά̆ν-δρῡς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠος</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a large kind of tunny</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pamphil.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				3.121b
			</span></i>:—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελάνδρυα</span></b>  (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεμάχη</span>),
				τά, <i>cheap cuts of tunny</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Xenocr.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				2.58.146
			</span></i> (said to resemble black oak-roots, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				9.48
			</span></i>); and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελανδρύαι</span></b> 
			(sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόμοι</span>), οἱ, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
			</span></i> l. c., <i><span class="en">
				7.315e
			</span></i>.</div>
